snapshot-from=router-for-me/models main on 2026-09-29: adds gpt-6.1-sol (codex-team/plus/pro and the Codex client catalog; free-plan accounts do not receive it, verified against chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/models with a free token), refreshes Codex client priorities/descriptions/plans, and takes upstream's claude-sonnet-5-5 row in place of the fork's hand-made one. Fork adjustment on top of the remote models.json: gpt-6.1-sol version is "gpt-6.1" (remote copy-pastes "gpt-6.0"). thinking.levels stay low..max even though the Codex client catalog lists "ultra": the backend rejects reasoning.effort=ultra on the wire ("Supported values are: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, and max", checked 2026-09-29), so ultra is a Codex CLI client-side mode and the proxy clamps it to max with a warning. The Codex client catalog is the remote file verbatim. Fork adjustment 2026-10-07: adds claude-haiku-5-5 to the claude section (released 2026-10-07 with Claude Code 2.1.293, which made it the default Haiku; 1M context, 128k output, adaptive thinking with effort low..max and a medium default, same tokenizer as 4.7+; cloned from the claude-sonnet-5-5 row because router-for-me/models main had no row for it as of its 2026-10-04 commit). Fork adjustment 2026-10-21 (v8.0.38 rebase): the thinking objects of claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-8, claude-fable-5, claude-fable-5-1, claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5 are taken from upstream v8.0.38's embedded models.json (ad9e456d, upstream issue 6698): sonnet-5-5 rejects thinking.type "disabled" and needs "between_tools"; opus-5-5, fable-5 and fable-5-1 cannot switch thinking off (zero_allowed false), so a request to disable it becomes low-effort adaptive, the none-to-lowest conversion the no-substitution design keeps; the adaptive models lose the budget min/max. Fork adjustment 2026-10-26 (v8.0.44 rebase): devin_models.json is upstream v8.0.44's embedded file verbatim (3dae075d folds the swe-2 lightning UIDs into one swe-2-lightning row;